@startuml
title Feature 002 - Teacher and Student UI Flow (After Core Acceptance)
start
:Teacher authorize Google account;
:Clear previous account data;
:Show own history + spreadsheet catalog;
if (Review saved activity?) then (yes)
  :Owner-only history detail from SQLite;
  :Show full names, answers, results, writeback status;
else (new)
  :Search / next page / select spreadsheet;
  :Preview first worksheet + mapping;
  :Set group count and create waiting activity;
  fork
    :Teacher table: group rows / question columns;
    :Full names wrap; long table scrolls;
    :Text for joined / unanswered / accepted / winner;
  fork again
    :Students choose group and required name;
    :Atomic join; name becomes immutable;
    :Waiting screen, no question content;
  end fork
  :Teacher opens activity;
  :Students see questions; submit complete groups;
  :Teacher live table updates after commits;
  :Teacher presses End and automatically fill answers;
  :Publish frozen results;
  :Automatic writeback status with text;
endif
if (Writeback needs recovery?) then (yes)
  :Explain authorization / verify / safe retry / conflict;
  :Allow only actions valid for current state and owner;
else (no)
  if (Still processing?) then (yes)
    :Show queued / writing text and live progress;
  else (no)
    :Show verified or no winning answers;
  endif
endif
:History remains after page close or service restart;
stop
note right
UI polish starts only after stories 1-4 pass.
Loading, empty and errors have text and actionable guidance.
1280x720, four groups, six questions, 40-character names.
Keyboard operation; status never relies on color alone.
end note
@enduml
